{"name":"Lanyard","hex":"#c09972","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lanyard","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A short rope used for fastening rigging, as a handle, etc.","A cord worn around the neck, shoulder, or wrist which is attached to a small object to be carried such as an identity card or security pass, key, knife, or whistle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lanyard"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lanyard","blocks":[{"text":"A lanyard is a length of cord, webbing, or strap used for attachment, carrying, restraint, retrieval, activation, or deactivation. Lanyards range from light-duty straps worn around the neck, shoulder, wrist, or belt for carrying items such as keys, identification cards or badges, and small electronic devices, to safety equipment used for fall restraint, confined-space retrieval, and dead man's switches."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Pfeifenschnur.jpg/330px-Pfeifenschnur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lanyard","wikidata":"Q174279"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Marlingspike.JPG/500px-Marlingspike.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Marlingspike.JPG/500px-Marlingspike.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A typical marlinspike with lanyard","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMarlingspike.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Lanyard_Woelfe_Freiburg.jpg/500px-Lanyard_Woelfe_Freiburg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Lanyard_Woelfe_Freiburg.jpg/500px-Lanyard_Woelfe_Freiburg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Light-duty webbing lanyard for attaching keys, with a metal clip similar to that of a leash","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALanyard_Woelfe_Freiburg.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Ubuntu_USB_lanyard.jpg/330px-Ubuntu_USB_lanyard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Ubuntu_USB_lanyard.jpg/330px-Ubuntu_USB_lanyard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A USB flash drive with a webbing lanyard that includes a safety break-away feature – a predetermined and in this case reattachable segment (in black) meant to prevent accidental strangulation when the lanyard is worn around the neck","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUbuntu_USB_lanyard.jpg"}],"sounds":{"lanyard":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/07/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-I_learned_some_phrases-lanyard.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/07/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-I_learned_some_phrases-lanyard.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-I_learned_some_phrases-lanyard.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/07/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-I_learned_some_phrases-lanyard.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-I_learned_some_phrases-lanyard.wav.ogg"}]}}}